{
 "_about": "(0.4.6) The weather (rpg.world.WeatherSystem). 'presets': every kind of weather the world knows - its rain, snow, hail, wind-borne sand, fog, wind (1 a strong wind, past it a gale), cloud, storm (how often lightning strikes), snow drifting over the ground, the sky's extra darkness, the air's tint, its temperature offset (C), how long it lasts in game hours [least, most] (it always ends on the hour, as the schedule's activities do), its group, whether it happens of itself ('natural': false - only a console or a story brings it), and which weathers it may only follow ('after'). 'climates': each region's own cycle - its temperature and its swing from night to day, and how likely each weather is there (fog likelier at dawn, thunder in the afternoon). 'realms' and 'regions' say which climate rules where (the realm first, else the wild region); 'default' everywhere else. 'groups' says how a weather leans toward the next: from a group, each other group's weight is multiplied.",
